      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand he feels fine now, but that's exactly the trap with a TIA — symptoms often completely disappear, which doesn't mean the danger is gone. About 1 in 3 people who have a TIA will eventually have a full stroke, often within days, and those early hours matter enormously for treatment options. Migraine and stress wouldn't typically cause one-sided face and arm numbness appearing simultaneously. Please don't wait — call emergency services or get him to an ER right away, and let the doctors be the ones to rule out the serious cause.",
